Z||000000||RobertVol||12-18-2001||10:35 PM||||Well I know there have been threads on this and I want to comment on the Centerforce Dual Friction Clutch that Archie is selling...I know he uses this for his V-8 applications but I installed one on my stock 88 gt...<P>The pedal effort is much better and the Clutch hangs on for all its worth!!! I love it!!!<P>I know that there is a break-in period, and since mine was failing I had to get used to the improvement so that I would not be jaded. But the newness has worn off and I STILL LOVE IT!!!! IT GRABS in all gears and when you down shift....<P>BAM! instant power.. I love it...!!!!!<P>I just wanted Archie to know....its a good product and I am a happy customer....so if the thread gets started again you will know I have it and it works great... you really get what you pay for and I will say its alot more expensive than the LUK clutches and the like but this clutch is much better!!<P>Rob is out!!!! <P>Thanks for the space Cliff!<P>------------------<BR>Robert<BR>88GT 56k T TOP  <BR>North Florida Fiero Club<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Untitled-24.jpg">  <P><A HREF="http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros" TARGET=_blank>http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros</A>||||reg||7
Z||000001||GT GT 87||12-18-2001||10:48 PM||||Boy , that is good to hear about archie's CF . I have one , ready to be installed w/rebuilt engine (3.2,cam,etc.)You know , this clutch is made by CF for only Archie .I can't wait .||||reg||1
Z||000002||RobertVol||12-18-2001||10:51 PM||||I think you will enjoy it.....I know I am! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||Tina||12-18-2001||11:18 PM||||To take it a step further here.<BR>Had mine in the car now for last 6 month, and <BR>happy to report that when we did the "Annual Engine removal"(Don't ask, it's an Eric thing.)<BR>Centerforce looked like just like it did coming out of the box.<P>Tina  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||LZeitgeist||12-19-2001||08:17 AM||||Mine felt great in the car briefly, until my clutch hydralics took a crap... but I love the Centerforce!<P>RobertVol - your clutch pedal/hydraulic system is all stock, right? And it still operated the Centerforce with ease? Just wanting to make sure...<P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||RobertVol||12-19-2001||12:36 PM||||LZ----<P>Yep! its all stock....the only thing replaced last year was a bad slave but replaced with stock replacement. <P>The break in period left me with air in the line and I had a hard time with third gear but that worked itself out and now shifts like brand new but with less effort in my opinion<p>[This message has been edited by RobertVol (edited 12-19-2001).]||||reg||1
